<title>UK: GECC sets C$100 million December 2002 bond.</title>
<headline>GECC sets C$100 million December 2002 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Toronto-Dominion.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP</p>
<p> AMT    C$100 MLN     COUPON     5.625     MATURITY    30.DEC.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.225   PAY DATE    01.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    99.60     SPREAD	+18 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/CA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.625     SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.0 PERCENT SEPTEMBER 2001 BOND</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
